  "yours": true,
  "scenario": {
    "narrative": "Patrick owns two auto repair shops, Shop 1 and Shop 2. Next quarter (60 working days) he will work at one of them every day. The history shows each past day at each shop: whether Patrick was there and how many cars the shop fixed. Patrick needs the two shops together to fix at least 3,750 cars next quarter. He can accept falling short 1 quarter in 10, but not more often. Which shop should he work at?",
    "params": {
      "reader": "Patrick",
      "unit": "cars fixed",
      "periodName": "quarter",
      "periodLength": 60,
      "periodUnit": "working days",
      "runs": 10000
    },
    "decisionRule": "Run the recipe 10,000 times; each run is one possible quarter. In each run, draw every node once, in order, and work out both options' results. For each option report the typical result (the middle of the runs), the likely range (from the 5% point to the 95% point of the runs), and the chance of falling short (the share of runs below 3,750 cars fixed). Recommend the option with the higher typical result among the options whose chance of falling short is at most 0.1. Also report how often the recommended option's result is higher than the other's in the same run."
  },
